Subject: [PATCH] Enable module mode for Go module subprocesses

The caller may be built and tested in GOPATH mode. Its GO111MODULE=off
must not disable the go list -m and go mod commands used to inspect and
prepare the copied module fixtures. Explicitly enable module mode and
keep workspace discovery disabled for these child processes.

This preserves every test assertion and the issue00023 golden output.
The upstream fixes for workspace and tool directives are already in
v0.6.1; neither overrides an inherited GO111MODULE=off.

Upstream: https://github.com/gostaticanalysis/testutil
Status: downstream; no corresponding upstream fix found on 2026-10-23

diff --git a/mod.go b/mod.go
index 32b68e6..5523c76 100644
--- a/mod.go
+++ b/mod.go
@@ -243,6 +243,8 @@ func modfilePath(t *testing.T, dir string) string {
 
 	var stdout bytes.Buffer
 	cmd := exec.Command("go", "list", "-m", "-f", "{{.GoMod}}")
+	// Module commands must work even when the caller uses GOPATH mode.
+	cmd.Env = append(os.Environ(), "GO111MODULE=on", "GOWORK=off")
 	cmd.Dir = dir
 	cmd.Stdout = &stdout
 	if err := cmd.Run(); err != nil {
@@ -349,7 +351,8 @@ func execCmd(tb testing.TB, dir, cmd string, args ...string) io.Reader {
 	tb.Helper()
 	var stdout, stderr bytes.Buffer
 	_cmd := exec.Command(cmd, args...)
-	_cmd.Env = append(os.Environ(), "GOWORK=off")
+	// Module commands must work even when the caller uses GOPATH mode.
+	_cmd.Env = append(os.Environ(), "GO111MODULE=on", "GOWORK=off")
 	_cmd.Stdout = &stdout
 	_cmd.Stderr = &stderr
 	_cmd.Dir = dir
